---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/page-layouts.css';
---

<Layout
title="Hire me — Mike Trounce"
description="Two ways to work with me — talk it through as a consultant, or have it built — plus where else to find out more about me."
>
<div class="options-page">
<a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Mike Trounce</a>

<h1>Hire me</h1>
<p class="intro">
Two ways this usually goes, depending on what you need.
</p>

<section class="content-section">
<h2><a href="/consultant">Consultant</a></h2>
<p>
Just talk to me, the way you'd talk to any consultant — about your dealflow, the leads coming in, what's working and what isn't. <a href="/consultant">More on how that works &rarr;</a>
</p>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
<h2><a href="/builder">Builder</a></h2>
<p>
Have me actually do the work we talked about — set up a CRM, get you onto Bark.com, fix the website, start the social media marketing. <a href="/builder">More on how that works &rarr;</a>
</p>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
<h2>Find out more about me</h2>
<p>
<a href="/about">About</a> for background, a CV, and a video introduction. <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/michael-trounce/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a> and <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@michaeltrounce3746" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube</a> for more. Instagram and X to follow once there's something worth posting there.
</p>
</section>

<p class="cta">
Got something worth building? <a href="mailto:trounceflow@gmail.com">trounceflow@gmail.com</a>
</p>
</div>
</Layout>

<style>
.cta {
padding-top: 1.5rem;
border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
color: var(--ink-soft);
}
.cta a {
font-weight: 700;
color: var(--ink);
text-decoration: none;
border-bottom: 2px solid var(--illus-a);
}
.cta a:hover {
color: var(--green);
}
</style>
